    'pie.arriba': 'Back to top',
    'sobre.alt': 'Portrait of Mireia Gutiérrez Águila',
    'sobre.p1': 'I\'m drawn to projects that combine conceptual and analytical thinking. I like to get involved, and I consider myself sociable and collaborative.',
    'sobre.p2': 'I started in tech by studying PHP programming, which opened the door to working as a QA Tester. After two years at The Knot Worldwide, I continued my QA career at Zitro, where I now combine that role with Product Manager.',
    'sobre.p3': 'Over the past year I have started programming video games, training in Godot, Unity and Unreal, and I have created a few games of my own.',
    'inicio.rol': 'QA Tester & Product Manager | Indie Game Developer',
    'inicio.bajar': 'Scroll down to About me',
    'inicio.verProyectos': 'View projects',
    'inicio.contacto': 'Contact',
    'exp.verMas': 'Read more',
    'exp.verMenos': 'Read less',
    'exp.game.empresa': 'Hobby · Personal project',
    'exp.game.periodo': 'Since November 2025',
    'exp.game.resumen': 'Training in Godot, Unity and Unreal, and creating my own games: Ecos, MitoCat and Feminist.',
    'exp.game.d1': 'In November 2025, thanks to W_i_dev, an amazing community that promotes the presence of women in the industry, I started game development in my free time. I began with a Godot tutorial to make a game for a 6-day jam, Ecos, a small platformer; later, I decided to try the other two most in-demand engines to get a broader view and see which one suited me best.',
    'exp.game.d2': 'I made a very varied game with Unity, MitoCat, mixing 2D, 3D, platforming, a shooter, different physics and a range of mechanics to learn as much as possible, after first taking C# courses. My latest project is Feminist, a mobile game made in Unreal, where I got started with Blueprints; I also tried to make it diverse to enrich my learning.',
    'exp.pm.periodo': '2025 – present',
    'exp.pm.resumen': 'Creating and managing the documentation of an internal backoffice web, coordinating requirements with design, operations and development, and defining improvements that make daily operations easier.',
    'exp.pm.d1': 'Combining my roles as Product Manager and QA Tester gives me a very close, up-to-date technical view of all the changes and improvements on the server side. This perspective has allowed me to lead initiatives with a direct impact on team efficiency and product quality.',
    'exp.pm.d2': 'I actively work to identify and understand the backoffice needs that each team detects —such as data visualization, logical safeguards on the server to prevent configuration errors, or compliance with jurisdiction-specific regulations—, adapting and steering the creation of new applications to meet them as well as possible.',
    'exp.pm.d3': 'I have notably improved the documentation, making it much more specific and technical, which the PHP and Design teams have valued very positively compared to the previous approach. I have also fostered a much more open, fluid and close communication channel with PHP Development and the server team, achieving much higher involvement in projects from both sides.',
    'exp.pm.d4': 'Thanks to this collaborative workflow, I have been able to propose substantial, important changes not only on the frontend but also directly on the server. Taking on more and more responsibility, I proposed and managed from scratch —for both the server and PHP sides— a large strategic project that is essential to the company.',
    'exp.qa.periodo': '2022 – present',
    'exp.qa.resumen': 'Designing and running test plans across Backend, Frontend and Backoffice, setting priorities, analysing the impact of changes and proposing improvements that make other teams more efficient.',
    'exp.qa.d1': 'As a QA Tester, my experience covers both corporate environments and product development. In my current role, I handle backend testing —of casino games as well as the backoffice and the company\'s internal websites—, and I also run frontend tests on the casino games themselves. Previously, I was the sole QA owner for mobile apps (Android and iOS).',
    'exp.qa.d2': 'On the technical side, I have driven automation projects to improve process quality: I used Selenium to test the company\'s backoffice website and I have also started initiatives with Cypress to strengthen game validations.',
    'exp.qa.d3': 'I never settle for the established way: I don\'t just look at what fails, nor assume something can\'t change just because "it has always been done that way". I always go one step further in search of improvement strategies and good organisation, making efficient methodologies available even to other teams. To do so, I encourage constant dialogue, organising meetings when needed, writing clear documentation and structuring tasks that make collaboration and workflow easier.',
    'exp.pm.ejemplo': 'See documentation example',
    'exp.qa.ejemplo': 'See test examples',
    'exp.knot.resumen': 'Manual review of a multinational\'s website and mobile version. In the last months, QA lead for all of the company\'s apps.',
    'exp.maestra.puesto': 'Teacher',
    'exp.maestra.empresa': 'Education, Generalitat de Catalunya',
    'exp.maestra.resumen': 'Introductory courses in educational robotics and programming. Digital training for teachers on using new technologies in the classroom. Team facilitation with projects in Drive, Trello and Slack.',
    'exp.maestra.d1': 'Although at first glance it may seem unrelated to my current tech career, my experience as a teacher is one of my greatest assets and gives me a distinctive perspective. Throughout my time in education, I worked mainly in schools based on project-based methodologies. Designing, planning and coordinating educational projects together with students and teachers was my daily routine, which gave me a very solid overall view of project structure, priority management and the vital importance of communication between teams.',
    'exp.maestra.d2': 'All of this pedagogical and organisational foundation is invaluable to me in my day-to-day work today, both in my role as Product Manager and in designing and managing AI agents, allowing me to structure complex flows, anticipate needs and coordinate teams efficiently.',
