    'flujo.1.t': 'Plan',
    'flujo.1.x': 'A specification before coding',
    'flujo.1.d': 'I wrote Portfolio.md: sections, texts, links, requirements and tone. It is what the agent checks before building anything, and it takes priority if anything contradicts it.',
    'flujo.2.t': 'Instruct',
    'flujo.2.p': 'CLAUDE.md · memory',
    'flujo.2.x': 'The agent\'s rules in every session',
    'flujo.2.d': 'In CLAUDE.md I set how to work: plan before code, one section at a time, comments in Spanish and every command explained, plus the palette and typography. Claude Code loads it at the start of every session, and its memory keeps the project state between sessions.',
    'flujo.3.t': 'Equip',
    'flujo.3.x': 'Design and testing, two tools',
    'flujo.3.d': 'I installed two skills from anthropics/skills: frontend-design, to look for a purposeful visual direction instead of a template, and webapp-testing, to test with Playwright. Their versions are pinned in skills-lock.json. The MCP standard was not needed: the site is static.',
    'flujo.4.t': 'Design',
    'flujo.4.p': 'Plan mode',
    'flujo.4.x': 'The agent proposes options',
    'flujo.4.d': 'Before coding, the agent shows me options: a sample with palette and typefaces, or several mock-ups of the section. I choose, and what is decided is saved in CLAUDE.md so it is not lost between sessions.',
    'flujo.alt.t': 'Propose alternative',
    'flujo.alt.x': 'Another option until I am convinced',
    'flujo.alt.d': 'If I am not convinced, I ask for another option with my changes: colours, order, texts or shape. It repeats until I like it, just like in the conversation with the agent to design this very diagram.',
    'flujo.5.t': 'Build',
    'flujo.5.p': 'Permissions',
    'flujo.5.x': 'Plan approved by me before coding',
    'flujo.5.d': 'The agent proposes a plan for the section and I approve or change it before it codes. Every terminal command is explained before it runs and needs my permission.',
    'flujo.5.q': 'I check that it does not make up data (anything not in Portfolio.md it has to ask me) and that it does not publish my phone number or references.',
    'flujo.rep.t': 'I report the bug',
    'flujo.rep.x': 'I reproduce it and demand tests that can fail',
    'flujo.rep.d': 'If something fails, I reproduce it and ask the agent to fix it. Then I demand a test that would have caught the bug and that proves it can fail.',
    'flujo.rep.q': 'Real example: the horizontal scroll in Skills overshot in Safari. WebKit and Firefox measured the width about 1700 px too large.',
    'flujo.6.t': 'Test',
    'flujo.6.x': 'Chromium, Safari and Firefox',
    'flujo.6.d': 'Playwright scripts in Chromium, WebKit (Safari) and Firefox, at several widths: contrast, keyboard, reduced motion, no JavaScript and languages.',
    'flujo.6.q': 'I require every test to prove it can fail: the agent had written checks that always passed, and now each one has a negative control.',
    'flujo.rev.t': 'I review and approve',
    'flujo.rev.x': 'The section in my browser, or I ask for tweaks',
    'flujo.rev.d': 'I look at the section in my browser: design, texts, translations and accessibility. If something does not convince me I ask for tweaks; if it is fine I approve it and we move on to the next one.',
    'flujo.rev.q': 'While sections remain, the cycle goes back to Design. When none are left, it moves on to the code review.',
    'flujo.rc.t': 'Code review',
    'flujo.rc.x': 'I go over every change and check that nothing important was deleted from Portfolio.md or CLAUDE.md',
    'flujo.rc.d': 'Before publishing I go over the changes (the diff) and check that nothing important was deleted from Portfolio.md or CLAUDE.md. I also watch for any private data slipping in.',
    'flujo.7.t': 'Publish',
    'flujo.7.x': 'One branch per phase, merges are mine',
    'flujo.7.d': 'One Git branch per phase and a Pull Request to review before merging. I make the commits, branches and merges; the agent only suggests what to include.',
